  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NSD in Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the wider British Red Cross localisation agenda, our team&#x2019;s vision is that by 2030, our Host National Societies in Asia will be better prepared and equipped to respond to emergencies, and be well-positioned with their governments, communities, and prospective donors to serve those most in need. It is for this reason that we have identified National Society Development (NSD) as a key strategic focus area for our region, and have dedicated regional resources to support this, in addition to the existing programmatic initiatives underway at a country level.
This project will allow us to make our NSD interventions greater than the sum of their parts, and to coordinate with IFRC and other PNS in ensuring our support to our HNS is as effective as it can be.</narrative>
  </description>
